# lint-copy.allow - quoted examples that scripts/lint-copy.mjs must not flag (DESIGN.md §3, D31).
#
# Format, one entry per line:   rule | path glob | needle | reason
#   rule       a rule id from `node scripts/lint-copy.mjs --list-rules`, or *
#   path glob  repository-relative; ** crosses directories, * does not
#   needle     text from the string, paragraph or line the finding came from (case and whitespace do not matter).
#              Never a line number: those go stale on every edit.
#   reason     required; say why the banned wording appears (e.g. "quoted as the example of what not to write")
# Use this only for quotation (a METHOD.md paragraph that shows the banned phrase as an example, a hostile-label
# fixture). Never use it to keep real copy that breaks a rule: reword the copy.
# An entry that matches nothing fails the full scan ("stale-allow"), so delete entries when the text they covered goes.
#
# The planning documents (the internal plan and notes, DECISIONS.md, research/) are not
# scanned at all because they define these rules by quoting them; see INTERNAL_DOC_GLOBS in lint-copy.mjs.
#
pct99 | docs/CONTRACT.md | a bare "no change" | the contract's copy-lint item lists the banned words as the rule's definition
nothing-changed-on-your-side | docs/CONTRACT.md | "proves", "caused by" | the contract's copy-lint item lists the banned words as the rule's definition
quality | plugin/skills/report/SKILL.md | counts are indicators, not a quality score | instruction to the model that names the banned framing in order to forbid it
score | plugin/skills/report/SKILL.md | counts are indicators, not a quality score | instruction to the model that names the banned framing in order to forbid it
quality | plugin-codex/skills/report/SKILL.md | counts are indicators, not a quality score | instruction to the model (Codex skill) that names the banned framing in order to forbid it
score | plugin-codex/skills/report/SKILL.md | counts are indicators, not a quality score | instruction to the model (Codex skill) that names the banned framing in order to forbid it
pct99 | design/demo-data.v2.json | shown as "range", never | the demo data's method note quotes the label the interface must never print (D31)
nerf | engine/src/cli/design-tokens.ts | nerf | the design system's own glance-banned pattern, copied verbatim (engine/test/output/design-sync.test.ts holds the copy to the source)
nerf | plugin/mod/design-tokens.ts | nerf | the design system's own glance-banned pattern, copied verbatim into the mod (plugin/tests/fixtures/sync.mjs --check holds the copy to the source)
